3. RESTful API (Intermediate)
Objective: Create a RESTful API using Go and serve it with an HTTP server.
Description:
Build a simple API (e.g., a user management system with endpoints to add,
 delete, and update users).

Use JSON for request/response handling.

Add validation, error handling, and use a lightweight database 
like SQLite or a file-based storage.

Skills Gained:
Building APIs using Go’s net/http package.
Working with REST principles (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE).
JSON serialization/deserialization.
Using SQLite or other lightweight databases.
